  "name": "FACTOR - X ACTIVITY STUART POWER",
  "code": "1542",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong data-start=\"72\" data-end=\"84\">Factor X</strong> is a vitamin K-dependent clotting factor essential for the <strong data-start=\"144\" data-end=\"162\">common pathway</strong> of the coagulation cascade. It is synthesized in the liver. The <strong data-start=\"227\" data-end=\"253\">Factor X activity test</strong> measures the functional activity of this clotting factor in plasma.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1190\" data-end=\"1219\"><strong data-start=\"1194\" data-end=\"1219\">Clinical Significance</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1221\" data-end=\"1258\"><strong data-start=\"1226\" data-end=\"1257\">Decreased Factor X Activity</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1259\" data-end=\"1722\">\n<li data-start=\"1259\" data-end=\"1431\">\n<p data-start=\"1261\" data-end=\"1331\"><strong data-start=\"1261\" data-end=\"1294\">Inherited Factor X Deficiency</strong> (rare autosomal recessive disorder):</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1431\">\n<li data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1431\">\n<p data-start=\"1336\" data-end=\"1431\">Severe deficiency may present with umbilical stump bleeding, mucosal bleeding, or hemarthrosis.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1432\" data-end=\"1722\">\n<p data-start=\"1434\" data-end=\"1454\"><strong data-start=\"1434\" data-end=\"1453\">Acquired Causes</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1457\" data-end=\"1722\">\n<li data-start=\"1457\" data-end=\"1483\">\n<p data-start=\"1459\" data-end=\"1483\"><strong data-start=\"1459\" data-end=\"1483\">Vitamin K deficiency</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1486\" data-end=\"1537\">\n<p data-start=\"1488\" data-end=\"1537\"><strong data-start=\"1488\" data-end=\"1505\">Liver disease</strong> (Factor X synthesized in liver)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1540\" data-end=\"1590\">\n<p data-start=\"1542\" data-end=\"1590\"><strong data-start=\"1542\" data-end=\"1590\">Disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1642\">\n<p data-start=\"1595\" data-end=\"1642\"><strong data-start=\"1595\" data-end=\"1625\">Oral anticoagulant therapy</strong> (e.g., warfarin)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1645\" data-end=\"1722\">\n<p data-start=\"1647\" data-end=\"1722\"><strong data-start=\"1647\" data-end=\"1662\">Amyloidosis</strong> (Factor X binds to amyloid fibrils, reducing plasma levels)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1724\" data-end=\"1761\"><strong data-start=\"1729\" data-end=\"1760\">Increased Factor X Activity</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1762\" data-end=\"1891\">\n<li data-start=\"1762\" data-end=\"1799\">\n<p data-start=\"1764\" data-end=\"1799\">Not usually clinically significant.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1800\" data-end=\"1891\">\n<p data-start=\"1802\" data-end=\"1891\">Occasionally associated with increased thrombotic risk, but not commonly tested for this.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1898\" data-end=\"1929\"><strong data-start=\"1902\" data-end=\"1929\">Associated Lab Findings</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1930\" data-end=\"2116\">\n<li data-start=\"1930\" data-end=\"1985\">\n<p data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"1985\"><strong data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"1957\">Prolonged PT and aPTT</strong> with low Factor X activity.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1986\" data-end=\"2018\">\n<p data-start=\"1988\" data-end=\"2018\">Normal <strong data-start=\"1995\" data-end=\"2017\">thrombin time (TT)</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"2019\" data-end=\"2116\">\n<p data-start=\"2021\" data-end=\"2116\">Liver function tests and vitamin K status should be evaluated in case of acquired deficiencies.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
